Loads the if_agnic kernel driver at boot so the front-panel ports of a Sophos
XGS desktop appliance (XGS 116/126/136 family, Marvell CN9130 NPU, PCI
11ab:7080) appear as port1..portN and can be assigned like any other NIC.

Also creates mvmgmt0, the PCIe management link to the NPU. Leave it
unassigned unless you need to reach the NPU; set hw.agnic.mvmgmt=0 in a
loader tunable to suppress it.

Requires a reboot to activate. Every frame is forwarded by the host; there is
no hardware offload. Per-model support status is documented in the project
repository; the XGS 116 is the upstream reference, the XGS 126 is this
plugin's target.

WWW: https://github.com/piorkowskim79/xgs-npu-freebsd
